counterfactuals.output:
1. A method for producing coated organic pigment microparticles, comprising:

introducing a pigment solution comprising an organic pigment dissolved in a solvent and a precipitation solvent for precipitating the organic pigment into a processing space formed between at least two processing surfaces that are capable of approaching and separating from each other;

mixing the pigment solution and the precipitation solvent in the processing space while at least one of the processing surfaces moves relative to the other, thereby precipitating organic pigment microparticles;

supplying, to the processing space or to a subsequent processing space, an oxide-coating precursor capable of forming a colorless transparent oxide; and

forming a coating comprising the colorless transparent oxide on surfaces of the precipitated organic pigment microparticles,

wherein the precipitation of the organic pigment microparticles and the formation of the coating are performed continuously.
